    "//harness-canvas-writers": [
      "FIVE HARNESSES DELETE INSIDE THE OPENED PROJECT'S `.aurora/canvas`, and they REQUIRE",
      "`S1DISASM_DIR` to name a WRITABLE COPY of a populated s1disasm. They are harness:canvas-cdp,",
      "harness:art-agent, harness:commit-cdp, harness:commit-collision and harness:constraints-cdp.",
      "There is deliberately NO DEFAULT. The default used to be the LIVE sibling checkout, so",
      "`npm run harness:canvas-cdp` with nothing set recursively deleted the canvas artwork stored",
      "in it (20 real files were sitting there on 2026-09-03). The guard is at the top of",
      "scratchpad/canvas-cdp-harness.mjs, refuses at import — before any rmSync — and refuses again",
      "if the variable is pointed at the live checkout anyway. d-28, COPY ONLY WHERE IT CAN WRITE.",
      "  cp -r <sibling>/s1disasm /tmp/s1disasm-copy",
      "  S1DISASM_DIR=/tmp/s1disasm-copy npm run harness:canvas-cdp",
      "The copy must be POPULATED: these harnesses open it and load GHZ act 1.",
      "Policed by `scripts/check-peer-path-literals.mjs` rule 5, peer-tree-write."
    ],
